messages:
Samir K: Quick Q — can we temporarily enable full request-body logging on /api/ingest to reproduce a customer error? Payloads are user docs, may include emails/SSNs. Need approval or safer suggestions.
Maria (sec): Short answer: do not log raw PII. If you absolutely must capture bodies, do it in staging only, redact known fields, restrict access, and set a short retention. Ping security for sign-off.
Alex G: We only see the bug when certain document structures exist; a redacted sample would help. Can we log the first ~8KB with field-level redaction (emails -> <REDACTED>, ssn -> <REDACTED>)?
Samir K: Proposed quick middleware snippet (will PR):
```
function redactBody(body) {
  if (!body) return body;
  if (body.email) body.email = '<REDACTED>';
  body.text = (body.text || '').replace(/\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g, '<REDACTED>'); // ssn
  // remove any model prompts/tokens
  if (body.prompt) body.prompt = '[REDACTED_PROMPT]';
  return body;
}
const safe = redactBody(req.body);
log.info('ingest.debug', { path: req.path, body: truncate(safe, 8192) });
```
Samir K: Also propose: strip Authorization header and other sensitive headers before logging.
Alex G: +1. Replace header value with 'Bearer <REDACTED>' before writing logs. Also consider logging a SHA256 of the raw doc so we can correlate without storing text.
Maria (sec): Good patterns. Add credit card regex and other country-variant SSNs. Must not log full prompts or API tokens. Access to these logs should be limited to security + the eng oncall, with explicit justification.
DevOps Bot: Audit: temp-logging-request created by Samir K for /api/ingest (id: TL-20260317-01). Expires: 7 days. Access: security, eng-oncall.
Jenna (support): tagging customer success for visibility — @Customer Success Bot do you need the redacted sample from the customer?
Customer Success Bot: Sent a secure upload link to the customer; will share a redacted sample to staging once available.
Maria (sec): Next steps: 1) PR with middleware + regex list + header strip + truncated logging 2) Put logs in ephemeral bucket with 7-day TTL and strict IAM + enable object-level encryption 3) Security review sign-off in PR. If all that is in place, I can approve staging logging for 48 hours. :+1:
Samir K: Will open PR today and tag @Maria (sec). We'll only enable in staging and follow the TTL + IAM rules. Thanks everyone. :white_check_mark:
